<title>USA: GPU's Homer City, Pa., coal unit back Wed.</title>
<headline>GPU's Homer City, Pa., coal unit back Wed.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>GPU Generation Inc said Tuesday it expected the 600 megawatt (MW) coal-fired unit 1 at its Homer City, Pa., power station to resume production on Wednesday after being shut Saturday for maintenance.</p>
<p>Pennsylania Electric Co (Penelec) and New York State Electric &amp; Gas Corp, each have a 50 percent interest in the Homer City unit 1.</p>
<p>Both Penelec and GPU Generation, which operates the Homer City facility, are subsidiaries of General Public Utilities Corp of Parisippany, N.J.</p>
<p>--R Leong, New York Power Desk +1 212 859 1622</p>
</text>
